Here's an irritation I'd like to have explained:

Sonya the Valkyrie is, like all of her previous incarnations, skipping
merrily along in the Gnomish Mines, bashing gnomes and dwarves with her
little dog Barfus.  Suddenly something invisible "touches" her!  She is
covered with frost, but doesn't get cold.  Big deal, right?  Well, a dwarf
and three gnomes happen along about this time...  The invisible
whatever-it-is "touches" her several more times (bad touch! bad touch!) and
she gets a headache, she starts getting confused, she starts getting hit by
it and the gnomes.  She's too confused to fight the wimps decently, and
seems to miss this thing every time she's pointed in the right direction.
Finally, besieged and unable to stagger back to the staircase, she falls, 
"Killed by a dwarf."  I had no way of figuring out what the thing was, and
was pretty P.O.'ed since this was one of my better-equipped characters.

Along comes the NEXT Sonya the Valkyrie.  Down into the Gnomish Mines.
Makes some friends in Minetown.  No big deal.  The next level down, right by
the staircase -- yep!  Something invisible "touches" her!  This time she
makes it back up the staircase to heal, but when she goes back down it taps
her again.  Worse, there's a carnivorous ape down there too, and a Titan, and
once confused she gets crushed very quickly.  This time it was the invisible
thing that finished her off -- and I find out what it is.  "Killed by an
invisible master lich."


Now.  My question.  What the <HADES> is an INVISIBLE MASTER LICH doing in
the Gnomish Mines?  Is there even a faint chance that it was randomly
generated, and not the result of a very bad polymorph trap?  (The presence
of the Titan suggests a poly trap and that I was very, very unlucky.)  Also,
twice in a row is a very bizarre coincidence.  Are monsters like that left
around in bones levels?  I thought it was just you, your stuff, and your
pets.

Needless to say, a "del bones*.*" followed in very short order.


Blessings, and I really dislike invisible master liches....

